From: TODO <TODO>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: Add Sony IMX241 (INT347F) to supported sensors

Not for upstream yet, and NOT applied by scripts/prepare.sh (it lives in
patches/pending/): there is no Linux driver for the IMX241 yet, and
ipu-bridge must only list sensors that are actually supported. Worse,
ipu3-cio2 creates its media links and subdev nodes only once every
sensor in the fwnode graph has bound (cio2_notifier_complete()), so
listing INT347F without a driver that binds would take the working rear
OV8858 camera down with it. Move this patch to patches/ together with
the sensor driver.

The Sony IMX241 is found with ACPI HID INT347F on IPU3 based devices
such as the HP Pro x2 612 G2, where it is the front camera on CSI-2
port 1 with 2 data lanes.

Add it to the list of sensors supported by ipu-bridge so that the
fwnode graph is built for it. The link frequency of 499.2 MHz is the
operating point of the Windows driver (19.2 MHz MCLK, pre-PLL divider
2, multiplier 104, PLL 998.4 MHz, RAW10 on 2 lanes). It is provisional:
with a 24 MHz MCLK (the TPS68470 clock is shared with the OV8858, which
needs 24 MHz) the nearest operating point is 498 MHz, and the driver
and this entry must agree on the value.

Signed-off-by: TODO <TODO>
---
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347A", 1, 360000000),
 	/* Omnivision OV7251 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347E", 1, 319200000),
+	/* Sony IMX241 */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347F", 1, 499200000),
 	/* Hynix Hi-556 */
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT3537", 1, 437000000),
 	/* Lontium lt6911uxe */
